      "claim": "The term 'fair trade' in standard historical and economic analysis implies voluntary participation and equitable terms between parties with relative agency, rather than mere adherence to local custom.",
      "evidence": "Modern definitions of fair trade emphasize ethical sourcing, fair wages, and the absence of exploitation; even historical economic analysis distinguishes between 'customary' exchange and 'fair' (equitable/voluntary) exchange.",
