      "claim": "Medieval English peasants (serfs/villeins) were legally bound to the land and subject to the lord's jurisdiction, lacking the legal capacity to freely negotiate terms or exit the relationship.",
      "evidence": "Historical records of the feudal system, including the Statute of Labourers and manorial court rolls, demonstrate that serfdom restricted mobility and forced labor services (corvée) were non-negotiable obligations.",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "depends_on": []
    },
