      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The economic interaction was characterized by extraction and coercion, where the lord set the terms of rent and labor, creating a structural power imbalance that precluded equitable negotiation.",
      "evidence": "Manorial records show that rents and labor demands were often increased unilaterally by lords, and peasants had no market leverage to refuse or renegotiate these terms without facing legal penalty or loss of livelihood.",
