      "answer": "Yes",
      "reason_rejected": "This position relies on the anachronistic interpretation that 'fair' simply means 'according to the custom of the time.' While exchanges were customary, the structural coercion and lack of voluntary agency inherent in serfdom mean they do not meet the standard criteria for 'fair trade' (equity and voluntary exchange). The devil's advocate attack on the definition of 'fair' fails because even under historical economic standards, the lack of agency distinguishes feudal obligation from fair trade."
